The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

channel1:

 3D Stokes problem in a channel with a square cross section. Computed is the
 developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow direction (x) and
 assuming periodical boundary conditions.

channel2:

 3D viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 Computed is the developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow
 direction (x) and assuming periodical boundary conditions.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration to steady state

channel3:

 3D viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 Computed is the developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow
 direction (x) and assuming periodical boundary conditions.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 first-order time integration to steady state

channel4:

 3D viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 Computed is the developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow
 direction (x) and assuming periodical boundary conditions.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration to steady state
 This problem is the same as channel2, but now using coupling of objects
 in realizing the periodical boundary conditions.

channel5:

 3D Stokes problem in a channel with a square cross section. Computed is the
 developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow direction (x) and
 assuming periodical boundary conditions.
 Navier-slip boundary conditions.
 Dirichlet normal wall velocity.
 Collocation for periodic boundaries.

channel6:

 Viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow).
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration to steady state

channel7:

 Viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow).
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration to steady state

channel8:

 Viscoelastic problem in a curved channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow). Axisymmetric.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration to steady state

channel9:

 Viscoelastic problem in a curved channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow). Axisymmetric.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration to steady state

channel10:

 Viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow).
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance.
 second-order time integration to steady state

channel11:

 Viscoelastic problem in a curved channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow). Axisymmetric.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance.
 second-order time integration to steady 

channel12:

 3D Stokes problem in a channel with a square cross section. Computed is the
 developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow direction (x) and
 assuming periodical boundary conditions. Prisms.

channel13:

 3D viscoelastic problem in a channel with a square cross section. 
 Computed is the developed flow using only one layer of elements in the flow
 direction (x) and assuming periodical boundary conditions.

 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration to steady state
 Prisms

channel14, channel14a:

 Viscoelastic problem in a curved channel with a square cross section. 
 3D velocities on a 2D domain (developed flow). Axisymmetric.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order time integration to steady state

 Similar to channel11 but now with a b-tensor formulation.
 NOTE: channel14 uses nodal point level rotation reinitialization.
       channel14a uses element level rotation reinitialization.
